    "referenceAnswer": "(a) 取撞向牆壁的方向為正。\n初動量 = 0.50 × 12 = 6.0 kg m s⁻¹\n末動量 = 0.50 × (−8.0) = −4.0 kg m s⁻¹\nΔp = −4.0 − 6.0 = −10 kg m s⁻¹\n即大小 10 kg m s⁻¹，方向與入射方向相反。\n\n(b) F = Δp / Δt = −10 ÷ 0.040 = −250 N\n即大小 250 N，方向與小球入射方向相反（指離牆壁）。\n\n(c) 說法錯誤。根據牛頓第三定律，牆壁對小球的作用力與小球對牆壁的作用力大小相等（250 N）、方向相反。牆壁近乎不動是因為其質量極大且與地面連結，由 a = F / m 可知加速度可忽略，並非因為所受的力較小。\n\n(d) F = Δp / Δt，Δp 不變（仍為 10 kg m s⁻¹），Δt 由 0.040 s 加倍至 0.080 s，故平均作用力減半，變為 125 N。\n安全氣囊的原理相同：氣囊延長乘客減速所需的時間，由 F = Δp / Δt 令平均作用力下降。須注意氣囊【不能】減少動量的變化 —— 乘客的動量最終同樣要由初值降至零，能改變的只有這個過程所用的時間。",
    "marks": 9,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) Take the direction towards the wall as positive.\nInitial momentum = 0.50 × 12 = 6.0 kg m s⁻¹\nFinal momentum = 0.50 × (−8.0) = −4.0 kg m s⁻¹\nΔp = −4.0 − 6.0 = −10 kg m s⁻¹\nThat is, magnitude 10 kg m s⁻¹ directed opposite to the incoming motion.\n\n(b) F = Δp / Δt = −10 ÷ 0.040 = −250 N\nMagnitude 250 N, directed opposite to the incoming motion (away from the wall).\n\n(c) The statement is wrong. By Newton’s third law the force of the wall on the ball and of the ball on the wall are equal in magnitude (250 N) and opposite in direction. The wall barely moves because its mass is very large and it is joined to the ground, so by a = F / m its acceleration is negligible — not because the force on it is smaller.\n\n(d) From F = Δp / Δt, Δp is unchanged (still 10 kg m s⁻¹) while Δt doubles from 0.040 s to 0.080 s, so the average force halves to 125 N.\nAn airbag works on the same principle: it lengthens the time over which the occupant decelerates, reducing the average force through F = Δp / Δt. Note that the airbag CANNOT reduce the change in momentum — the occupant’s momentum must still fall from its initial value to zero; only the time taken can be changed.",
    "contentEn": "A 0.50 kg ball hits a wall horizontally at 12 m s⁻¹ and rebounds along the opposite direction at 8.0 m s⁻¹. The collision lasts 0.040 s.\n(a) Find the change in momentum of the ball.\n(b) Find the average force exerted by the wall on the ball.\n(c) A student writes: \"the wall experiences a smaller force because it does not move.\" Comment on this statement.\n(d) If the collision time were extended to 0.080 s for the same change in speed, how would the average force change? How does this relate to the design of an airbag?",
    "explanationEn": "(a) The most frequent error is treating the change in momentum as m(12 − 8) = 2.0 kg m s⁻¹. Momentum is a vector; rebounding means the direction reverses, so a positive direction must be fixed first and signs substituted, giving m(−8.0 − 12) = −10 kg m s⁻¹. An error here carries straight through into (b).\n(c) This tests Newton’s third law. The force on the wall is equal in magnitude and opposite in direction to the force on the ball; the wall does not move because its mass is very large (and it is joined to the ground), so its acceleration is negligible — not because the force on it is smaller. Reading \"does not move\" as \"smaller force\" confuses the third law with the second.\n(d) From F = Δp / Δt, with Δp fixed and Δt doubled the average force halves. An airbag works exactly this way, by extending the collision time to reduce the force; it cannot reduce the change in momentum, since the occupant’s momentum must reach zero regardless.",
    "markingScheme": "(a) 3 分 —— 明確設定正方向（1）；反彈速度代入負值（1）；10 kg m s⁻¹ 連方向（1）。答 2.0 kg m s⁻¹ 者 (a) 全失。\n(b) 2 分 —— 正確使用 F = Δp / Δt（1）；250 N 連單位及方向（1）。\n(c) 2 分 —— 指出說法錯誤並引牛頓第三定律說明兩力大小相等（1）；以質量極大／加速度可忽略解釋牆壁不動（1）。\n(d) 2 分 —— 減半至 125 N（1）；指出氣囊延長碰撞時間而【不能】減少動量變化（1）。只寫「氣囊較軟所以較安全」不得分。\n本題所列分數為本平台練習用尺度，並非香港考試及評核局的分數分配。參考答案只列必達步驟與判準，刻意不提供可直接抄錄的完整答卷。交卷後請逐項對照自評，機器不會為本題評分。",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) 3 marks — a positive direction stated explicitly (1); the rebound velocity substituted as negative (1); 10 kg m s⁻¹ with direction (1). An answer of 2.0 kg m s⁻¹ loses all of (a).\n(b) 2 marks — correct use of F = Δp / Δt (1); 250 N with units and direction (1).\n(c) 2 marks — the statement identified as wrong, with Newton’s third law giving equal magnitudes (1); the wall’s immobility explained by its very large mass / negligible acceleration (1).\n(d) 2 marks — halved to 125 N (1); the airbag identified as extending the collision time and NOT reducing the change in momentum (1). \"The airbag is soft so it is safer\" earns nothing.\nThe marks shown are a practice scale used on this platform, not an HKEAA mark allocation. The reference answer lists the required steps and criteria rather than a copyable model script. Compare your own work against it point by point; nothing here is machine-marked.",
    "suggestedMinutes": 15
